# Template for /opt/graph-agent-core-dev/.env on the dev droplet (deploy/terraform/dev): the whole dev stack on one machine, with a hosted LLM instead of the laptop's Ollama.
# Create it on the droplet, by hand: `make droplet-sync` never copies a .env, so a laptop's keys do not travel. Everything else the dev stack reads has a default (the repository's
# .env.example lists it); only the model endpoint is yours to say. Production's counterpart is deploy/prod/prod.env.example, with the same LLM_* names, in the same order.
# Every variable deploy/dev/hosted-llm.yml reads is listed here (tests/core/test_env_examples_match_compose.py).

# --- LLM access (deploy/dev/hosted-llm.yml: LiteLLM on a hosted endpoint, running deploy/prod/litellm-config.yaml) ---
# The upstream model: any OpenAI-compatible endpoint. The example targets OpenAI; swap in Anthropic's OpenAI-compatible endpoint, a hosted vLLM, etc.
LLM_API_BASE=https://api.openai.com/v1
LLM_API_KEY=
LLM_CHAT_MODEL=openai/gpt-4o-mini
LLM_EMBED_MODEL=openai/text-embedding-3-small
# Optional middle and strong tiers (the `chat-medium` and `chat-strong` aliases). Unset = the chat model, so the proxy always starts. To attach one, set all three of its lines and restart
# the proxy (deploy/prod/prod.env.example says how, and what to state in the config's `model_info` if LiteLLM does not know the price).
# LLM_MEDIUM_CHAT_MODEL=
# LLM_MEDIUM_API_BASE=
# LLM_MEDIUM_API_KEY=
# LLM_STRONG_CHAT_MODEL=
# LLM_STRONG_API_BASE=
# LLM_STRONG_API_KEY=
